WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.919 --> 00:00:12.383
On September 19th, 1991,
two hikers traversing the Ötzal Alps

00:00:12.383 --> 00:00:17.305
on the border of Austria and Italy
discovered a corpse emerging from the ice.

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:20.266
Researchers soon realized they weren’t
looking at the victim

00:00:20.266 --> 00:00:23.269
of a recent climbing accident,
as initially assumed,

00:00:23.269 --> 00:00:29.484
but the mummified body of a man
who’d lived about 5,300 years ago,

00:00:29.484 --> 00:00:32.445
who they came to call Ötzi the Iceman.

00:00:35.823 --> 00:00:41.079
One early theory for Ötzi’s alpine death
was that he was a local shepherd or hunter

00:00:41.079 --> 00:00:43.748
who got caught in bad weather and froze.

00:00:43.873 --> 00:00:48.294
However, a shocking discovery eventually
revealed his true cause of death

00:00:48.294 --> 00:00:50.088
and upended his story.

00:00:50.129 --> 00:00:53.132
So, what do we know about Ötzi?

00:00:53.132 --> 00:00:54.634
And how did he die?

00:00:55.051 --> 00:00:59.680
Over the millennia, the Alpine cold 
and sun protected Ötzi’s body

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:03.434
from decomposition, 
freezing and drying it out in cycles,

00:01:03.434 --> 00:01:05.978
and leaving critical clues
for researchers.

00:01:06.395 --> 00:01:11.651
Ötzi was about 160 centimeters tall,
weighed some 50 kilograms,

00:01:11.651 --> 00:01:14.570
and died between 40- and 50-years-old.

00:01:15.029 --> 00:01:18.908
He led an active life but had
a strong genetic predisposition

00:01:18.908 --> 00:01:20.952
for cardiovascular diseases.

00:01:20.952 --> 00:01:24.330
His intestines were also parasitized
by whipworms

00:01:24.330 --> 00:01:27.125
and his stomach contained
ulcer-causing bacteria,

00:01:27.125 --> 00:01:30.795
all of which might have caused
some unpleasant symptoms.

00:01:31.379 --> 00:01:34.966
He died hundreds of years before
Stonehenge and the Great Pyramid

00:01:34.966 --> 00:01:39.804
were constructed, around 3350 BCE.

00:01:39.929 --> 00:01:43.391
Ötzi lived during the late
Neolithic Copper Age,

00:01:43.391 --> 00:01:45.810
when metal extraction
and crafting practices

00:01:45.810 --> 00:01:47.687
were spreading throughout Eurasia.

00:01:47.687 --> 00:01:50.731
Indeed, along with stone arrowheads
and knives,

00:01:50.731 --> 00:01:54.861
Ötzi carried an axe made of copper
from what is now Tuscany.

00:01:55.361 --> 00:01:58.447
Swaths of his clothing were made
of sheep and goat leather,

00:01:58.447 --> 00:02:00.950
and his diet included cultivated grains,

00:02:00.950 --> 00:02:05.830
all of which suggested that Ötzi’s people
relied on certain domesticated animals

00:02:05.830 --> 00:02:06.873
and crops.

00:02:07.123 --> 00:02:09.667
And when researchers 
inspected Ötzi’s skin

00:02:09.667 --> 00:02:12.461
with light ranging from infrared to UV,

00:02:12.753 --> 00:02:15.965
they found a total of 61 tattoos.

00:02:16.132 --> 00:02:19.635
Interestingly, the markings corresponded
with areas of Ötzi’s body

00:02:19.635 --> 00:02:21.846
where he probably experienced pain,

00:02:21.846 --> 00:02:26.142
like from degeneration observed
in his knees, ankles, and spine.

00:02:26.475 --> 00:02:30.229
Researchers think that the tattoos
might have been intended as treatment—

00:02:30.229 --> 00:02:33.149
perhaps an early form of acupuncture.

00:02:33.566 --> 00:02:37.904
Close scrutiny also clarified
the circumstances of Ötzi’s death—

00:02:37.904 --> 00:02:41.282
and led to a tantalizing prehistoric
murder mystery.

00:02:41.490 --> 00:02:46.495
A decade into studying Ötzi,
a CT scan picked up a crucial detail:

00:02:46.495 --> 00:02:50.708
there was a flint arrowhead lodged
in Ötzi’s left shoulder.

00:02:50.750 --> 00:02:55.504
Soon enough, researchers started piecing
Ötzi’s final days together.

00:02:56.047 --> 00:03:00.301
A deep cut wound on Ötzi’s hand
showed initial signs of healing

00:03:00.301 --> 00:03:03.137
and must have occurred
just days before his death.

00:03:03.179 --> 00:03:06.891
It was likely a defensive wound
which indicated that Ötzi was attacked

00:03:06.891 --> 00:03:10.353
with a sharp blade
but fought back and survived.

00:03:10.603 --> 00:03:13.147
Ötzi may have dressed
the wound with bog moss,

00:03:13.147 --> 00:03:17.026
which has antiseptic properties
and was found with his remains.

00:03:17.109 --> 00:03:21.530
Meanwhile, the types and location
of pollen in Ötzi’s digestive tract

00:03:21.530 --> 00:03:24.242
indicated that it was spring
or early summer

00:03:24.242 --> 00:03:26.911
and that his last three days were hectic.

00:03:27.161 --> 00:03:30.331
Ötzi seemed to be fleeing something.

00:03:30.498 --> 00:03:33.042
About 33 hours before his death,

00:03:33.042 --> 00:03:36.921
Ötzi was at an altitude
of around 2,500 meters,

00:03:36.921 --> 00:03:38.047
near the timber line.

00:03:38.047 --> 00:03:40.925
Then, approximately 24 hours later,

00:03:40.925 --> 00:03:46.764
he descended to at least 1,200 meters,
to a zone of warmth-loving trees.

00:03:46.931 --> 00:03:51.686
In his final hours, Ötzi reached
an altitude of around 3,000 meters

00:03:51.686 --> 00:03:55.564
where grasses, sedges,
and certain wildflowers dominated.

00:03:55.982 --> 00:04:02.363
His last meal included a large helping
of dried wild ibex, roe deer, and grains.

00:04:02.780 --> 00:04:06.409
Then, despite Ötzi’s apparent efforts
to escape the conflict,

00:04:06.409 --> 00:04:10.246
someone at a distant vantage
shot him from behind.

00:04:10.454 --> 00:04:15.001
The arrow pierced a major artery
and embedded itself in his left shoulder,

00:04:15.001 --> 00:04:17.169
causing extensive blood loss.

00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:19.463
Ötzi probably died soon after,

00:04:19.463 --> 00:04:24.427
his remains and all his belongings left
undisturbed in the glacier for millennia.

00:04:24.927 --> 00:04:31.642
This 5,300-year-old cold case has offered
invaluable glimpses into the distant past.

00:04:31.726 --> 00:04:35.938
But the mystery of who exactly Ötzi was
and why he was killed

00:04:35.938 --> 00:04:37.940
will probably never be solved—

00:04:37.940 --> 00:04:42.153
the tangible evidence for the act
degraded and carried away,

00:04:42.153 --> 00:04:45.614
lost to snow drifts long ago.

